module std_method_body.neg_1

// ONE seeded cause: `to_ascii_lower` is a std method whose SIGNATURE novac read
// and whose BODY the shell novac links against does not carry (measured
// 2026-09-05 by probe: the shell's surface has `byte_len`, `to_ascii_upper`,
// `starts_with`, not this one), so the call names a symbol nothing defines.
// Since 274.7 B1b-1 a std method the shell DOES carry is an ordinary interop
// call -- `byte_len`, this fixture's carrier until that day, compiles now --
// so the seeded cause moved to a method the shell lacks. The subset says this
// by name instead of emitting C that cannot link.
//
// The local below is the CASCADE probe, and it is the point of this fixture:
// until 2026-08-20 the gate "was anything refused?" asked the file's whole
// diagnostic count, so a refusal HERE made `@type_bind` skip its `@scope.bind`
// in `main`, and `n` came back as a second, false diagnostic -- "unknown name"
// about a name that is bound one line above.
fn lower(s str) -> str => s.to_ascii_lower()

fn main() {
    ro n = 1
    println(n)
}
